  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Codex Enterprise Analytics",
      "description": "This API allows ChatGPT Enterprise and Codex administrators to pull daily Codex\nadoption and code review metrics for a workspace. It is intended for dashboarding,\nreporting, and trend analysis, with metrics aggregated by day and optional per-user\nbreakdowns where available. The endpoints return time-ordered pages with\ncursor-based pagination.\n\n## Authentication\n1. Create a Platform API key at https://platform.openai.com/settings/organization/api-keys.\n2. Email support@openai.com to add the `codex.enterprise.analytics.read` scope and\n   remove all other scopes.\n3. Send requests with `Authorization: Bearer <platform_api_key>`.\n4. The base URL is `https://api.chatgpt.com/v1/analytics/codex`.\n\n## Finding your workspace ID\nChatGPT Admins and Codex Admins can open the ChatGPT Admin console at\nhttps://chatgpt.com/admin and copy the org ID and Workspace ID from the workspace\nsettings page.\n\n## Pagination and request parameters\n- `start_time` and `end_time` define the reporting window in Unix seconds (end_time\n  is exclusive).\n- `limit` controls page size.\n- `page` is the cursor token from a previous response's `next_page`.\n\nResponses are ordered by `start_time` ascending and return a page envelope with\n`object`, `data`, `has_more`, and `next_page`. When `has_more` is true, pass\n`next_page` back as the `page` query parameter to fetch the next set of rows.\n"
    }
  ]
}